hadiths[13]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1894","[AI-translation] Hadith of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that Allah, the Almighty, continued to send revelation to His Messenger before his death until He took him while the revelation was most abundant. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away afterwards.""
"1895","Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab:\n\n Once a Jew said to me, \O the chief of believers! There is a verse in \n your Holy Book Which is read by all of you (Muslims) ""1896"",Narrated `Urwa bin Az-Zubair:\n\nThat he had asked `Aisha about the meaning of the Statement of Allah: \If you fear that you shall not \nBe able to deal justly With the orphan girls"""
"1896","[AI-translation] Zubair, that he asked Aisha about the saying of Allah, the Almighty, (And if you fear) to (and fourth). She said: O son of my sister, she is the orphan girl who is in the custody of her guardian, sharing with him in his wealth, and her wealth and beauty please him, so her guardian wants to marry her without being fair in her dowry, giving her like what another would give her. Thus, they were forbidden to marry them unless they are fair to them, and give them the highest of their customary dowry, and they were commanded to marry other women who please them. Aisha said: Then the people asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after this verse, so Allah revealed (And they ask your ruling concerning women) to His saying (And you desire to marry them). And what Allah mentioned as being recited to you in the Book is the first verse in which He said, (And if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphan girls, then marry those that please you of other women). Aisha said: And the saying of Allah in the other verse, (And you desire to marry them), refers to the desire of one of you for his orphan girl who is in his custody, when she has little wealth and beauty. They were forbidden to marry those among the orphan women whose wealth and beauty they desired, except with fairness, because of their turning away from them.""
"1897","Narrated Hisham bin `Urwa from his father:\n\nwho heard Aisha saying, \The Holy Verse; 'Whoever amongst the guardians is rich"""
"1898","Narrated Aisha:\n\nRegarding the explanation of the following verse:-- \If a wife fears Cruelty or desertion On her \nhusband's part.\"" (4.128) A man may dislike his wife and intend to divorce her"""
"1899","Narrated Sa`id bin Jubair:\n\nThe people of Kufa disagreed (disputed) about the above Verse. So I went to Ibn `Abbas and asked \nhim about it. He said, \This Verse:-- \""And whoever kills a believer intentionally"""
"1900","Hadith of Ibn Abbas: Ibn Abza said: Ibn Abbas was asked about Allah's saying: ""And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell..."" [4:93], and His saying: ""And those who do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right..."" [25:68] until it reached ""except those who repent..."" [25:70]. So I asked him, and he said: ""When it was revealed, the people of Mecca said: 'We have associated partners with Allah, killed the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, and committed indecencies.' So Allah revealed: 'Except those who repent, believe, and do righteous deeds...' until His saying: 'Forgiving, Merciful.'"""" ""1901"",Narrated Ibn `Abbas:\n\nRegarding the Verse: \And say not to anyone who offers you peace (by accepting Islam)"""
"1901","[AI-translation] Hadith of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding (And do not say to one who greets you with peace, ""You are not a believer""). He said: A man was with a small flock of his, and the Muslims encountered him. He said, ""Peace be upon you,"" so they killed him and took his flock. Allah revealed concerning that, up to His saying, (goods of the worldly life) — that is the flock.""
"1902","A man came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, ""I am ruined!"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him, ""What is the matter?"" He said, ""I have done a sexual relation with my wife (while fasting) in Ramadan."" The Prophet said to him?"" ""Can you afford to manumit a slave?"" He said, ""No."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Can you fast for two successive months?"" He said, ""No."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Can you feed sixty poor persons?"" He said, ""No."" Then an Ansari man came with an Irq (a big basket full of dates). The Prophet said (to the man), ""Take this (basket) and give it in charity."" That man said, ""To poorer people than we, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)? By Him Who has sent you with the Truth! There is no house in between the two mountains (of the city of Medina) poorer than we."" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said (to him), ""Go and feed it to your family."""" ""1903"",This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Ibn 'Umar through another chain of transmitters"""
"1903","[AI-translation] Hadith of Ibn Mas'ud, regarding (to their Lord the means). He said: There were people from among mankind who used to worship people from among the jinn. The jinn embraced Islam, but these people held fast to their religion.""
"1904","I asked Ibn 'Abbds r-+t. ru ,j: about Sftrat At-Taitoa, and he said, Sfirat ArTauba? It is the exposure (of all the evils of the infidels and the hypocrites). And it continued revealing (the oft-repeated expression): '... and of them ... and of them'"""
"1905","A son of one of the daughters of the Prophet (ﷺ) was dying, so she sent a person to call the Prophet. He sent (her a message), What ever Allah takes is for Him"""
"1906","It was narrated that Hudhaifah said:The Messenger of Allah said: 'I know what the Dajjal will have with him. He will have two flowing rivers, one that appears to the eye to be clear water, and one that appears to the eye to be flaming fire. If anyone sees that, let him go to the river which he thinks is fire and close his eyes, then lower his head and drink from it, for it is cool water. The Dajjal has one blind eye, with a layer of thick skin over it, and between his eyes is written ""disbeliever,"" which every believer will read, whether he is literate or illiterate"""
